@snap_left_nominee_ready
title: A named Left compromise goes to the Sejm
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_dem_candidate_left = 1;
Q.snap_dem_base =
    Number(Q.democratic_committed_seats) +
    Number(Q.left_committed_seats) -
    Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) * 0.08) +
    Math.round((Number(Q.other_seats) || 0) * 0.20);
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 1;
Q.snap_dem_left_support = 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica nominates " + Q.snap_dem_candidate + " for prime minister";
!}

**[+ snap_dem_candidate +]** leads a Left programme with **[+
snap_dem_base +]** expected votes.

- @snap_left_nominee_vote

@snap_left_nominee_vote
title: Put the named compromise to a vote
go-to: snap_dem_vote

@snap_democratic_role
title: Define Lewica's relationship to the nominee
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0; snap_dem_left_support = 0

**[+ snap_dem_candidate +]** has **[+ snap_dem_base +]** expected votes
outside Lewica. Supporting the investiture does not by itself put Lewica in
government; cabinet entry requires a separate coalition agreement.

- @snap_dem_join
- @snap_dem_supply
- @snap_dem_oppose

@snap_dem_join
title: Join the cabinet and accept collective responsibility
subtitle: Adds every committed Lewica vote and grants governing capacity only if the cabinet wins.
choose-if: snap_dem_candidate_left = 1 or coalition_viable_left_ko = 1
unavailable-subtitle: KO and Lewica are too far apart, in trust and in programme, to sign a cabinet agreement; supply and confidence remain available.
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_dem_base +=
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0);
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 1;
Q.snap_dem_left_support = 1;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica signs a coalition agreement with the Sejm nominee";
!}
go-to: snap_dem_vote

@snap_dem_supply
title: Vote confidence from opposition under a written supply pact
subtitle: Adds the same votes, but grants no ministries or state-budget capacity.
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_dem_base +=
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0);
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0;
Q.snap_dem_left_support = 1;
Q.razem_dissent -= 4;
Q.barons_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica offers confidence and supply without cabinet entry";
!}
go-to: snap_dem_vote

@snap_dem_oppose
title: Withhold Lewica's votes
subtitle: The nominee must find 231 without the Left.
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment = 0;
Q.snap_dem_left_support = 0;
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica withholds its votes from the Sejm nominee";
!}
go-to: snap_dem_vote

@snap_dem_vote
title: Sejm-led cabinet vote
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const roll = Math.floor(
    (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 9
) - 4;
Q.snap_dem_variance = roll;
Q.confidence_candidate = Q.snap_dem_candidate;
Q.confidence_yes = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        460,
        Math.round(Number(Q.snap_dem_base) || 0) + roll
    )
);
Q.confidence_abstain = Math.min(
    460 - Q.confidence_yes,
    18,
    4 + Math.abs(Math.min(0, roll))
);
Q.confidence_no = Math.max(
    0,
    460 - Q.confidence_yes - Q.confidence_abstain
);
Q.confidence_present = 460;
Q.confidence_threshold = 231;
Q.government_has_confidence = Q.confidence_yes >= 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.confidence_mode = "Post-snap Sejm second attempt";
if (Q.government_has_confidence) {
    Q.prime_minister = Q.snap_dem_candidate;
    Q.prime_minister_intro_return = "ministries_or_event_queue";
    Q.prime_minister_intro_pending = 1;
    Q.government_name = Q.snap_dem_candidate + " democratic cabinet";
    const leftLedSnapCabinet =
        Number(Q.snap_dem_candidate_left) == 1;
    Q.government_party = leftLedSnapCabinet ? "lewica" : "ko";
    Q.government_owner = leftLedSnapCabinet
        ? Q.left_party_name
        : "KO-led democratic coalition";
    Q.left_in_government =
        Q.snap_left_cabinet_commitment ? 1 : 0;
    Q.position = Q.left_in_government
        ? "Governing coalition"
        : (
            Q.snap_dem_left_support
                ? "Confidence-and-supply opposition"
                : "Parliamentary opposition"
        );
    Q.coalition_status = Q.left_in_government
        ? "Sejm-elected democratic coalition cabinet"
        : "Sejm-elected cabinet with external Lewica support";
    Q.coalition_seats = Math.min(
        Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460,
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.democratic_committed_seats) || 0) +
        (Q.left_in_government
            ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)
            : 0)
    );
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        Number(Q.democratic_committed_seats) || 0
    );
    Q.caretaker_government = 0;
    Q.formation_complete = 1;
    Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
    Q.budget = Q.left_in_government ? 3 : 0;
    Q.budget_authority = Q.left_in_government
        ? "Post-election coalition reserve"
        : "Opposition — no state spending authority";
    Q.left_cabinet_committed =
        Q.left_in_government ? 1 : 0;
    Q.left_cabinet_model = Q.left_in_government
        ? (
            leftLedSnapCabinet
                ? "Programme-bound cooperating Left entry"
                : "New Left ministers · Razem external support"
        )
        : (
            Q.snap_dem_left_support
                ? "Confidence and supply from opposition"
                : "Opposition"
        );
    Q.ministries_finalized =
        Q.left_in_government ? 0 : 1;
    Q.ministry_allocation_mode = Q.left_in_government
        ? "formation"
        : "settled";
    Q.ministry_return_mode = "event_queue";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.snap_dem_candidate + " wins the Sejm's cabinet vote";
} else {
    Q.caretaker_government = 1;
    Q.early_election_risk = 100;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The Sejm's second attempt fails and a third presidential attempt remains";
}
!}

= Second confidence roll call

**[+ snap_dem_candidate +]: [+ confidence_yes +] yes · [+
confidence_no +] no · [+ confidence_abstain +] abstain**

Yes count: **[+ snap_dem_base +] negotiated base** + **[+
snap_dem_variance +] roll-call variance**. Threshold: **231**.

[? if government_has_confidence: The Sejm elects its own cabinet after the
President's nominee fails.?]
[? if not government_has_confidence: The third stage remains. It uses a
simple majority of votes cast; only failure there requires another election.?]

- @snap_return_2026
- @snap_post_election_third

@snap_return_2026
title: Record the formed government
view-if: government_has_confidence = 1
on-arrival: snap_election_requested = 0
go-to: poland_prime_minister_intro.show

@snap_post_election_third
title: Proceed to the President's third attempt
view-if: government_has_confidence = 0
on-arrival: snap_formation_context = "Post-election formation"; snap_formation_attempt = 3; news_headline = "The post-election formation enters its final constitutional attempt"
go-to: snap_formation_attempt_three


@airspace_standing_review
title: Convert the record into a standing parliamentary security review
subtitle: Requires the command-continuity file opened in 2023. Turns four years of separate incidents into one permanent institution.
choose-if: defence_command_response = "Operational record demanded" or defence_command_response = "Brokered continuity statement" or defence_command_response = "Joint opposition demand"
unavailable-subtitle: There is no continuous command record to build on — the 2023 vacancy was answered with a campaign argument, not a file.
on-arrival: {!
Q.airspace_response = "Standing security review";
Q.security_incident_pressure = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.security_incident_pressure) || 0) - 10
);
Q.defence_readiness =
    (Number(Q.defence_readiness) || 46) + 8;
Q.civil_military_trust =
    (Number(Q.civil_military_trust) || 50) + 8;
Q.institutional_trust =
    (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 6;
Q.administrative_capacity = (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) +
    (Q.left_in_government ? 3 : 1);
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_national_security_support += 7;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "A standing parliamentary review replaces four years of separate incidents";
!}

The 2023 file, the drone incursions, the border, the sabotage arrests and this
month's fragments go into one standing review with a fixed reporting cycle, a
cross-party membership and a duty on the services to appear. It is the
institution that should have existed in 2022 and was never built because every
incident was answered on its own.

Officers who have spent four years being quoted selectively by whichever camp
found it useful now have a venue that outlasts a news week. So does the next
government, whoever forms it.

- @poland_event_queue: Establish the standing review
